!---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Users should add all user specific MOM_input parameter changes after
! these comments as follows:
!   parameter_name = new_parameter_value
!
! If the parameter belongs to a parameter block, enter it within the
! block, or prefixed with the block name, e.g., change N_SMOOTH within
! the KPP block as follows:
!   KPP%
!   N_SMOOTH = 3
!   %KPP
! or:
!   KPP%N_SMOOTH = 3
!
! Note: The parameter changes added to this file will automatically be
!       applied to:
!   $RUNDIR/MOM_override
!
! The diag_table may be changed via lines of the form
!   diag_table%<stream>%<key> <operator> <value>
! where <stream> is the name of an output file, e.g., h.native for the
! files ${CASE}.mom6.h.native.*.nc, and <key> is fields, module, or a
! file setting (see param_templates/diag_table.yaml), e.g.:
!   diag_table%h.native%fields += MLD_0125, Kd_heat:Kd_heat_max:max
!   diag_table%h.native%fields -= KE
!   diag_table%h.sfc%output_freq = 5
!   diag_table%h.z%fields = none
! Fields are given as name[:output_name[:reduction]], and are removed
! by output name. A new stream also needs the diagnostics module of its
! fields (ocean_model, ocean_model_z or ocean_model_rho2), e.g.:
!   diag_table%h.mine%module = ocean_model_z
!   diag_table%h.mine%fields = thetao, so
!
! WARNING: If a MOM_override file is placed in SourceMods/src.mom/,
! any additional parameter changes in this file will trigger an error,
! and so will diag_table changes if a diag_table (or
! diag_table.unresolved) file is placed there.
